  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Telmatochromis temporalis is a medium-sized cichlid (10-12 cm). It has a rather dull coloration and is quite robust in its behaviour. A dwarf variety, the \"shell\" form, only grows to 5-6 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species settles along the whole of Lake Tanganyika.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Snail-cichlids are a specialty of Lake Tanganyika. Nowhere else are so many specialized species found. In the lake there are real fields of empty snail shells. Shells that lie here and there, more or less solitary, are settled by specialized snail-cichlids such as Lamprologus ocellatus. Where fields of empty shells exist, they are also used by species that are usually regular cave brooders. A dwarf variety of T. temporalis has developed in areas where large snail-shell fields occur.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Quite robust in its behaviour.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>A typical cave brooder with a parental family.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25b-perchlike-fishes-2-cichlids-from-the-great-african-lakes/telmatochromis_temporalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species is not very popular in the hobby because of its rather dull coloration. The dwarf form reaches only 5-6 cm. It is currently considered conspecific with the normal form, which is why it is given the additional name \"shell\" in the hobby. In contrast to the normal form, this dwarf is highly sought after, because its unusual shape adds a very interesting aspect to any community tank for Tanganyika cichlids.</p>"
    }
  ],
